# Build artifacts MUST use '**' — in .containerignore '*' does NOT cross
# '/', so a bare '*.elc' excludes ONLY root-level files.  Nested artifacts
# (lisp/**/*.elc, src/*.o, deps/**/*.so, ...) then leak into the build
# context and an incremental in-container `make` ships them STALE — e.g. a
# tramp-compat.elc byte-compiled under an older Emacs version, which then
# warns "Tramp has been compiled with Emacs X, this is Emacs Y" even though
# the C was rebuilt fresh.  No binary artifacts are tracked in git, so the
# in-container build regenerates all of these.
native-lisp
**/*.elc
**/*.eln
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/*.so
# Generated pkg-config files (deps/{cad-glib,ai-glib,libreclaw}/*.pc) are
# build artifacts, never tracked in git.  If a host-generated one leaks
# into the context it shadows the in-container probe -- notably
# cad-glib-1.0.pc, whose Libs.private libregnum reads via sed: a stale
# host pc carrying -lTKernel (built where opencascade was present) makes
# the container link OCCT toolkits that aren't installed there.  Excluding
# them forces cad-glib's `all` (which has the .pc as a prerequisite) to
# regenerate them from the container's own probe.
**/*.pc
src/*.pdmp
src/emacs
src/temacs
src/bootstrap-emacs*
tools/cmacs-mcp/cmacs-mcp
# CMake build dirs bake an ABSOLUTE host path into CMakeCache.txt.  If a
# host build tree leaks into the context, in-container cmake aborts with
# "source does not match ... used to generate cache".  whisper.cpp is
# configured+built by the cmacs `make' via CMake, so never copy its host
# build tree (and drop any stray CMake cache).
deps/whisper.cpp/build
**/CMakeCache.txt
# gcc -MMD dependency files record ABSOLUTE paths to the headers of the
# machine that compiled them.  Leaking a host .d into the context makes
# in-container make demand a header that distro does not have, and the
# error names the missing FILE rather than the stale .d:
#
#   No rule to make target '/usr/include/glib-2.0/gio/giptosmessage.h',
#     needed by 'build/debug/objs/driver/sqlite/orm-sqlite-driver.o'
#
# That header is new in glib 2.86.  Fedora 44 and Arch have it, so their
# images built fine; Fedora 43 and Ubuntu 24.04 do not, and died in a
# dependency nobody edited.  ~1900 of these exist in a built tree.  None
# are tracked in git and every one is regenerated by the in-container
# compile, so excluding them is free.
**/*.d
# CMake export/config fragments in a dep's build tree bake in host paths
# for the same reason.
**/build/**/*.cmake
# Podman also reads .gitignore which has a blanket Makefile rule.
# Negate the Makefiles that are hand-written (not generated by configure).
!cmacs/bacon/modules/Makefile
!cmacs/gsurf/modules/Makefile
!tools/cmacs-mcp/Makefile
